From e8494d150289f5b17880616a21a3b171a261ce95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Junod <donujp@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:14:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Autogain: add a maximum gain setting

The autogain plugin raises the level of quiet material by as much as it
takes to reach the target, limited only by the peak of the signal, so a
quiet passage or an input that is just above the silence threshold can be
amplified by several tens of dB. There was no way to bound that.

Add the Maximum Gain setting, in dB, which limits the amplification only.
Reducing the level is not limited. The default of 100 dB is the largest
difference there can be between the target and the silence threshold, so
the default leaves the behavior unchanged.

The smoothing moves into autogain::smooth_gain(), which clamps the gain that
was applied to the last block to the limit before it smooths it, so lowering
the limit takes effect at once instead of decaying from the old gain. The
peak ceiling is unchanged.

The setting is saved in presets as maximum-gain. Presets without it get the
default, and the property list of the local server is updated.

autogain_gain_test checks that the default gives the same result as the
smoothing of c5dcd37a, and covers the limit, the peak ceiling, lowering the
limit and out of range values.
